.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-BUCKET-GET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-bucket-get - Show the team's bucket and its uses


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team bucket get <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the team's bucket: its endpoint, region, bucket name, folder prefix, access key ID and when Paperboat last wrote, read and deleted a check object in it. The secret access key is stored encrypted and is never shown, by this command or anywhere else.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-bucket(1)\fP
